#/texts/7.full_gt_text:
1. Shri Uma Shankar Dikshit assumed the office of Minister of Works and Housing;
2. Shri H.N. Bahuguna assumed the office of Minister (of State) of Communications;
3. Prof. D.P. Chattopadhyaya assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Health and Family Planning;
4. Shri Niti Raj Singh Chaudhury relinquished the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Petroleum, Chemicals and Non-Ferrous Metals and assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Law and Justice;
5. Shri D.R. Chavan relinquished the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Petroleum, Chemicals and Non-Ferrous Metals and assumed the office of Minister (of State) of Supply;
6. Shri Mohan Dharia assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Planning;
7. Shri K.R. Ganesh relinquished the office of Deputy Minister in the Ministry of Finance and assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Finance;
8. Shri I.K. Gujral relinquished the office of Minister of Works, Housing and Urban Development and assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Works and Housing;
9. Shri Shah Nawaz Khan assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Steel and Mines;
10. Dr. (Smt) Sarojini Mahishi relinquished the office of Deputy Minister in the Ministry of Tourism & Civil Aviation and assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Tourism & Civil Aviation;
11. Shri Chanshyam Bhai Oza assumed the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Industrial Development;
12. Shri Prakashchand B. Sethi relinquished the office of Minister of State (Defence Production) in the Ministry of Defence and assumed the office of Minister of Petroleum and Chemicals;
13. Shri V.C. Shukla relinquished the office of Minister of State in the Ministry of Finance and assumed the office of Minister of State (Defence Production) in the Ministry of Defence.
